      "text": "The modified interface will resist TGO spallation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Y-doped and annealed CrMnFeCoNi bond coats will form a thinner TGO than untreated CrMnFeCoNi bond coats.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Y-doped and annealed CrMnFeCoNi bond coats will form a more adherent and stable TGO than untreated bond coats.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The thinner and more adherent TGO will improve coating durability and reliability under thermal cycling.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Untreated CrMnFeCoNi bond coats typically form a thicker, less adherent TGO that is prone to rapid oxidation and spallation.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is expected to remain effective during moderate thermal cycling between approximately 400°C and 1100°C in air or combustion atmospheres.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Effectiveness may diminish under more extreme thermal conditions or after prolonged exposure that causes microstructural instability.",
